<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> When the price is \($x\) per download, what is the revenue in thousands of dollars? </para>
      </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> \(x(18-x)\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Is the relationship between the price of the movie and the revenue (in thousands of dollars) linear, quadratic, or exponential? Explain how you know.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
    <para>It is quadratic. The output \(x(18-x)\) can be written as \(18x-x^2\), which is a quadratic expression.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

